<!--
    A pointer parameter read only at field offsets of 0x1000 or more
    (`option ptrfromuse`, `kuna_ptrfromuse.rs (const_base_evidence)`).

    Issue: `p->field` and `table[i]` lower to the same INT_ADD of a value and a
    constant, and ptrfromuse's walk treated every constant at or above the data
    space's pointer lower bound (0x1000 on x86-64 and AArch64) as a possible
    global address. A parameter dereferenced only at such offsets never reached
    its loads, so it stayed an integer, and in a shared object whose first
    function sits at 0x1000 the field read at that offset printed as
    `*(int4 *)&near_leaf[a0]`, a subscript of a function.

    Stage / sub-stage: P5 type recovery, the `ptrfromuse` seed. When the image
    reports its data sections (the `globalref` ranges), a constant in none of
    them and not in code is a field offset, and so is a function's entry in
    code; a data section, and the rest of code, keep the old grades, and an
    image that reports no sections keeps them all (`kuna-ptrfromuse.xml`).

    Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/field-offset-pointers/` (built from `fields.c`,
    see its README): an x86-64 shared object, the same object stripped, an
    x86-64 non-PIE executable and an AArch64 shared object. `page_leaf` reads
    fields at 0x1000 and 0x1004, `conn_leaf` at 0x48a0..0x48a8, `near_leaf` at
    0xff8 and 0xffc (below the bound, the control). `get_data`, `put_bss`,
    `get_code` and `get_local` index a `.data`, a `.bss`, a `.text` and a local
    `.bss` table, unnamed in the stripped object, with their parameter, which
    stays an integer. In the AArch64 object `code_table` sits at 0x450, below
    the bound, where `get_code`'s parameter was a pointer before this change.
    `code_only_x86_64.so` (`code_only.c`) has no data section at all, and its
    one function, `update`, sits at 0x1000 and reads its record there.
    `absolute_x86_64.so` and `absolute_x86_64.o` (`absolute.c`) are the
    controls for the two limits: `read_reg` reads a peripheral-style absolute
    address 0x40020000 past 1 MiB, `letter_rank` indexes a byte table at the
    start of `.rodata` from a character (`&letters - 0x61`, just below the
    section), and in the relocatable object `get_ext` indexes an extern table
    whose slot sits outside every section. Each parameter stays an integer.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
